.TH MABOX-SNAPSHOT 1 "2026-08-23" "mabox-snapshot @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mabox-snapshot \- snapshot a running Mabox Linux system into a bootable live/install ISO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mabox-snapshot
.RI [ -h ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mabox-snapshot
builds a bootable live/install ISO from the currently running Mabox Linux
system. It is modeled on MX Linux's
.B mx-snapshot
but is not a port of it -- Mabox is Manjaro-based, with its own repo
layering, versioned multi-kernel packaging, and desktop bootstrap
(jgmenu/tint2/openbox) that a generic Arch tool doesn't account for.
.PP
Two build modes are supported:
.TP
.B preserving
A full personal clone: real /home, real accounts, real passwords. For
migrating to new hardware or backing up your own machine, not for sharing.
Optionally LUKS2-encrypted with
.BR --encrypt .
Calamares' own account-creation step is skipped, since the snapshot already
.I is
your account.
.TP
.B reset
A sanitized ISO for sharing: a synthetic demo/demo account replaces the real
user, no real /home, no saved network credentials, no machine ID.
.PP
.B calamares
is the live-ISO installer and an optional dependency -- it is normally
removed once Mabox is installed to disk. When it is not present on the
build host,
.B create
skips all Calamares branding and configuration and builds a
.I live-only
ISO: it boots to a live session but has no installer. The build prints a
notice when this happens; install
.B calamares
first for an installable ISO.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS version
Print the installed version.
.SS doctor
Check prerequisites (required tools, disk space, detected kernels).
Read-only, no root needed.
.SS "create {preserving,reset} [options]"
Build a snapshot. Requires root.
.TP
.B preserving | reset
Build mode; required positional argument. See DESCRIPTION above for what
each mode does.
.TP
.BR -w ", " --workdir " " \fIDIR\fR
Scratch directory for build state -- squashfs layers, ISO tree, mkinitcpio
config (default: /var/lib/mabox-snapshot/work).
.TP
.BR -o ", " --skip-space-check
Skip the free-space precheck on workdir/output-dir before building.
.TP
.B --output-dir \fIDIR\fR
Directory the finished ISO is written to (default: same as --workdir).
.TP
.B --iso-name \fINAME\fR
Base filename for the ISO, without .iso (default: mabox-<mode>-<timestamp>).
.TP
.B --compression {zstd,xz,lz4,lzo,gzip}
Squashfs compression algorithm passed to mksquashfs -comp (default: zstd).
xz compresses smallest but slowest; gzip is a universal fallback with a
weaker ratio; lz4/lzo are fastest but produce the largest output.
.TP
.B --compression-level \fILEVEL\fR
Compression level passed to mksquashfs -Xcompression-level. Only zstd
(1-22, default 15), gzip (1-9, default 9), and lzo (1-9, default 8) support
this -- xz and lz4 have no such option and will error if a level is given.
.TP
.B --exclude-list \fIFILE\fR
Path to a custom exclude-pattern file, replacing the default list (default:
/etc/mabox-snapshot/excludes.list).
.TP
.B --exclude-folder {Desktop,Documents,Downloads,Music,Pictures,Videos,Public,Templates}
Exclude a named XDG user folder from the snapshot in addition to
--exclude-list; repeatable.
.TP
.B --kernel \fINAME\fR
Only include this installed kernel, matched against mkinitcpio presets
(default: newest installed kernel).
.TP
.B --all-kernels
Include every installed kernel instead of just the newest.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the resolved plan and commands, execute nothing.
.TP
.B --explain
Print a plain-language walkthrough of what the build will do instead of the
raw commands, execute nothing.
.TP
.B --change-threshold-mb \fIMB\fR
Prompt about home-dir items new/grown by at least this many MiB since the
last snapshot (default: 200).
.TP
.B --encrypt
Encrypt rootfs.sfs with LUKS2 (preserving mode only; passphrase prompted
interactively at build time).
.TP
.B --profile {full,lean}
Size/completeness tier: full (default) or lean, which trims unselected
kernels' module trees plus VM/container storage.
.TP
.BR -n ", " --no-checksums
Skip writing a .sha256 checksum file alongside the ISO.
.SS "config {show,path,set}"
Inspect or edit the cascading TOML configuration (built-in defaults ->
system file -> user file -> CLI flags). Config keys match CLI flag names
with dashes replaced by underscores, e.g.
.B --output-dir
becomes
.BR output_dir .
.TP
.B show
Print the resolved config.
.TP
.B path
List config files in load order.
.TP
.BI "set " key " " value
Set a key in the user config.
.SS "excludes {list,edit,add,remove,reset,folders,backups,rules}"
Manage what a snapshot excludes.
.I /etc/mabox-snapshot/excludes.list
and
.I /etc/mabox-snapshot/overrides.list
are root-owned, so every subcommand that writes to them needs
.BR sudo ;
.B list
,
.B folders
,
.B "backups list"
,
.B "backups save"
, and
.B "rules list"
are read-only and need no root.
.TP
.B list
Print the current exclude list. Read-only, no root.
.TP
.B edit
Open the exclude list in $EDITOR. Root required.
.TP
.B reset
Restore the shipped default exclude list. Root required. Always saves a
timestamped backup of the list it's about to replace first (see
.B backups
below), so this is never a one-way trip.
.TP
.B folders
List named XDG folders and their resolved paths. Read-only, no root.
.TP
.BI "add " pattern
Add an mksquashfs -ef exclude pattern, relative to /, e.g. var/cache/*.
Root required.
.TP
.BI "remove " pattern
Remove a pattern, as printed by
.BR "excludes list" .
Root required.
.TP
.B "backups {list,save,restore}"
Saved copies of the exclude list, under
.IR ~/.config/mabox-snapshot/excludes-backups .
.B reset
writes one automatically; a named
.B save
doubles as a reusable custom template you can
.B restore
later.
.RS
.TP
.B "backups list"
List saved backups and named templates. Read-only, no root.
.TP
.BI "backups save " "[name]"
Save the current exclude list as a backup. With a name, it becomes a
reusable template (e.g.
.BR vm-heavy );
omitted, it's timestamped instead. Read-only, no root -- reads the
world-readable
.I excludes.list
and writes only to your own home.
.TP
.BI "backups restore " name
Restore the exclude list from a saved backup or template, as printed by
.BR "excludes backups list" .
Root required.
.RE
.TP
.B "rules {list,add,remove,clear,edit}"
Ordered include/exclude override rules, for keeping one subpath inside an
otherwise-excluded directory (e.g. one folder under Documents).
.RS
.TP
.B "rules list"
Print the current override rules. Read-only, no root.
.TP
.BI "rules add " action " " pattern
.I action
is
.B exclude
or
.BR include ;
.I pattern
is a path relative to /, e.g. home/*/Documents (glob allowed on exclude
rules only). Root required.
.TP
.BI "rules remove " action " " pattern
Remove a rule, as printed by
.BR "excludes rules list" .
Root required.
.TP
.B "rules clear"
Remove all override rules. Root required.
.TP
.B "rules edit"
Open the override-rules file in $EDITOR. Root required.
.RE
.SS "packages list [--explicit|--aur|--local|--all]"
List installed packages, read-only, no root needed. --explicit lists
explicit repo packages (default); --aur lists foreign packages reproducible
from the AUR; --local lists foreign packages found in neither; --all
combines all three.
.SS "skel audit [--home \fIDIR\fR] [--show-identical]"
Reporting only -- nothing here changes what a snapshot captures. Diffs your
home directory against the vendored mabox-skel baseline to show what's
untouched, customized, deleted, or fully your own. Use the 'differs' list
to decide what's worth protecting with
.B "excludes rules add include ..."
in a leaner snapshot profile.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mabox-snapshot/mabox-snapshot.conf
System-wide config.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mabox-snapshot/mabox-snapshot.conf
Per-user config, takes precedence over the system file.
.TP
.I /etc/mabox-snapshot/excludes.list
Default exclude list, editable via
.BR excludes .
.TP
.I /etc/mabox-snapshot/overrides.list
Ordered include/exclude override rules, editable via
.BR "excludes rules" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/mabox-snapshot/excludes-backups/
Exclude-list backups and named templates, managed via
.BR "excludes backups" .
.TP
.I /etc/mabox-snapshot/images/splash.png
Optional custom GRUB boot menu background; auto-resized/cropped to
1920x1080 if present.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mabox-snapshot/work
Default scratch/work directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check prerequisites, then build a full personal backup to a mounted USB
drive:
.RS
.nf
mabox-snapshot doctor
sudo mabox-snapshot create preserving --output-dir /mnt/usb --encrypt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build a sanitized ISO to share, with every installed kernel:
.RS
.nf
mabox-snapshot create reset --output-dir /mnt/usb --all-kernels
.fi
.RE
.PP
Persist a backup destination, then keep one subpath inside an
otherwise-excluded directory:
.RS
.nf
mabox-snapshot config set output_dir /mnt/backups/mabox-snapshots
sudo mabox-snapshot excludes rules add exclude 'home/*/Documents/*'
sudo mabox-snapshot excludes rules add include home/*/Documents/keep-this
.fi
.RE
.PP
Save the current exclude list as a reusable template, then restore it later:
.RS
.nf
mabox-snapshot excludes backups save vm-heavy
mabox-snapshot excludes backups list
sudo mabox-snapshot excludes backups restore vm-heavy
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non-zero on error.
.B doctor
also returns non-zero if any prerequisite check fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and source:
.I https://github.com/musqz/mabox-snapshot
.SH AUTHOR
musqz
